{"title":"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/3/9a38ccd7bebcd6e9086e42c1e9dcb6e2d95970c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x^{4} + ax^{3} + bx^{2} + cx + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"247\" height=\"19\" /> has real coefficients, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/3/d935758fdc88079e80fb122b82bcdf3975e511d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2i) = f(2 + i) = 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" /> What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/0/3609992cb62090c9ffa52cc0730cece92f9bfc2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c + d?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c66983d26396563fed3188dca0e655854412bf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 9 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A fourth degree polynomial has four <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Root\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Root\">roots</a>. Since the coefficients are real(meaning that complex roots come in conjugate pairs), the remaining two roots must be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_conjugate\" title=\"Complex conjugate\">complex conjugates</a> of the two given roots. By the factor theorem, our roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7c9aed0bc1a732053db0938c79dbc9248e7c5ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-i,-2i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />. Now we work backwards for the polynomial:\n</p>\n<div style=\"text-align:center;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a2892d359087ed1923e128f7eb8ca5a29178df5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-(2+i))(x-(2-i))(x-2i)(x+2i) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"354\" height=\"18\" /><br />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/6/076fbe48577ba10c0d68a0f480ebd552e8f5bf65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2 - 4x + 5)(x^2 + 4) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"201\" height=\"19\" /><br />\n</p>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a46838b90acb80b3df33c37320d99d5ad1d974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4 - 4x^3 + 9x^2 - 16x + 20 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"240\" height=\"16\" /></div>\n<p>Thus our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32d21baa12274267c99eec464d6ccd8549e27b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$- 4 + 9 - 16 + 20 = 9\\ \\mathrm{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Just like in Solution 1 we realize that the roots come in conjugate pairs. Which means the roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bf59023ced3d93343c5b561bb81cd79fec98566.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2i,i+2,-2i,2-i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"143\" height=\"16\" />\nSo our polynomial is  \n</p><p><b>(1)</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/f/5ef29ff13864ab8479edc6e0d3650231c7a04687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = (x-2i)(x+2i)(x-i-2)(x-2+i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Looking at the equation of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/bebb998361742138f397bc1629c91c1911ea90dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x^4+ax^3+bx^2+cx+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"247\" height=\"19\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e87eb4e245e8c12e256fcde96208ee1e5b1cf175.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d = f(1)-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"190\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>If we plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> into equation <b>(1)</b> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/1/de133dd4be3168b8ad05941acf3b003363d042d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) = (1-2i)(1+2i)(-1-i)(-1+i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"310\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Now if we multiply a complex number by its conjugate we get the sum of the squares of its real and imaginary parts. Using this property on the above we multiply  and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bcb36f74a08d153da1678009318e16cb08abfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) = (1-2i)(1+2i)(-1-i)(-1+i) = (1^2+2^2)(1^2+1^2) = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"516\" height=\"19\" />\nSo the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10df38dcd8c1f517a39b5857f978cd9f3127412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) -1 = 10 - 1  = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e88dc32d72b800739cb3736b1ccaa5c08d18eda3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\framebox{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WgySLk2p5VU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WgySLk2p5VU</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A\">2007 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/w